86086181 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "40a3f90a-5606-5f21-9444-7efba36a199f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086182 #edb/ref 1080 "1.321" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086182 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086182 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6683b2b6-bc11-5d63-9a9c-82de11e77232" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086183 #edb/ref 1080 "0.856" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086183 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086183 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7f117552-88ca-5863-8469-88b09dabfb56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086232 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086232 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086232 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086232 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086232 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086232 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086232 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086232 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186546463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186086232 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "78e69158-c06d-564e-b789-ce6a0691bb72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087494 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4103" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087494 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $x$ if $e^{x - 3}=2^5?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087494 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e22ac55-3e84-5cb4-8231-5f882da9240e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087494 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we take the natural logarithm $\\left(\\ln\\right)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-3} & ={2}^{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x-3}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\ln \\left( e^a \\right) = a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx-3 = \\ln \\left( 2^5 \\right).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$ and rewrite the right-hand side using the power law of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5}) \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5})+3 \\\\ x & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5\\ln (2) + 3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087495 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4104" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087495 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution to the equation $e^{2-4x} = 2$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087495 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ccf59ef2-a5dd-5a56-9af8-1878376dea16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087495 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(\\ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2-4x} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2-4x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 2-4x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ -4x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx  \\approx 0.327\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087496 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4105" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087496 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $e^{x+1} + 1 = 3,$ what is the value of $x$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087496 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "12eedc57-11a6-540c-bdc9-bf5df777de60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087496 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the exponential, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+1}+1 & =3 \\\\ {e}^{x+1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $\\left(\\ln\\right)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+1} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x+1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x+1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x =\\ln\\left(2\\right) -1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087689 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/r