b/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088254 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186086178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088254 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66592" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088254 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088254 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution to the equation ${e}^{y}=7$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088254 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "70d22aee-cf89-5d3c-9988-c197ae387fe1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088254 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088254 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y} & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny≈1.946\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088263 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186086232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088263 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66908" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088263 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088263 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that ${e}^{2w+1}+2=6,$ then $w=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088263 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4eca039f-43fe-568b-a212-c61f9bbcb6e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088263 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088263 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2w+1}+2=6 \\\\ {e}^{2w+1} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $w:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2w+1} & =4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2w+1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) \\\\ 2w+1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) \\\\ 2w & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-1 \\\\ w & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $w=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operato