86546898 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546898 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546898 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546898 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546898 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546898 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186546292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546898 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a12fa105-d919-568d-aa42-9d5dd1b4d2a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546937 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546937 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546937 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546937 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546937 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546937 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546937 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546937 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186546574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546937 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dffe3c5c-ed39-5c84-b167-5dd49aa3722c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546947 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546947 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546947 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546947 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186546668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546947 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eca758fe-2328-5a7b-bbea-03982c4511de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546961 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546961 #edb/ref 1069 "q-100280" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546961 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546961 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $y$ if ${e}^{7-y}=\\sqrt[7]{10}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546961 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "06bb1232-0a8a-5e1c-9d8b-cb06e8535b98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186546961 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7-y} & =\\sqrt[7]{10} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{7-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[7]{10})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n7-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[7]{10})\n$$\n\nNext, we write $\\sqrt[7]{10}$ as ${10}^{1/7}.$ So, we get:\n\n$$\n7-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({10}^{1/7})\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the right-hand side using power law of logarithms and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({10}^{1/7}) \\\\ 7-y & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\ -y & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-7 \\\\ y & =7-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=7-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547019 #edb/ref 1069 "q-263174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547019 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547019 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${e}^{-y/4}+6=14,$ then $y≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547019 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "75357678-4591-5397-a921-c421db4eafd8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547019 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y/4}+6 & =14 \\\\ {e}^{-y/4} & =14-6 \\\\ {e}^{-y/4} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y/4} & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-y/4}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ -\\frac{y}{4} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ y & =-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny≈-8.318\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547056 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547056 #edb/ref 1069 "q-100276" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547056 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547056 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $y$ if ${e}^{5-y}=\\sqrt[4]{7}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547056 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0fb4c30-2477-5421-b3da-f8a97304168e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547056 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5-y} & =\\sqrt[4]{7} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{5-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{7})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n5-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{7})\n$$\n\nNext, we write $\\sqrt[4]{7}$ as ${7}^{1/4}.$ So, we get:\n\n$$\n5-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{1/4})\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the right-hand side using power law of logarithms and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{1/4}) \\\\ 5-y & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ -y & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-5 \\\\ y & =5-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=5-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547080 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547080 #edb/ref 1069 "q-66937" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547080 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547080 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution to the equation ${e}^{z}=5$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547080 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f830d198-6965-5666-82fb-312c594f3381" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547080 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{z} & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{z}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz≈1.609\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
